Package: itsne
Title: Interval t-SNE for Interval-Valued Data
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      given = "Han-Ming",
      family = "Wu",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      email = "hanmingwu1103@gmail.com"
    )
  )
Description: Nonlinear dimension reduction and visualization for
    interval-valued observations, in which each observation is a
    hyperrectangle rather than a point, as studied in symbolic data
    analysis (Billard and Diday, 2006, <ISBN:9780470090169>). Four
    extensions of t-distributed stochastic neighbor embedding (van der
    Maaten and Hinton, 2008, <https://jmlr.org/papers/v9/vandermaaten08a.html>)
    are provided. Two expansion-based variants replace each interval by
    vertex or quantile representatives (Ichino, 2011,
    <doi:10.1002/sam.10113>) and reconstruct a reduced-space interval
    afterwards: 'itsne_vm()' and 'itsne_qm()'. Two direct variants
    optimize the reduced-space interval itself, either through coupled
    lower and upper endpoints with a soft order penalty, 'itsne_mm()', or
    through a center-radius parameterization with a Wasserstein-type
    distance (Irpino and Verde, 2008, <doi:10.1016/j.patrec.2008.04.002>)
    that guarantees positive radii, 'itsne_cr()'. Unlike baselines that
    embed derived point-valued features, the direct variants return an
    explicit interval-valued embedding. Interval principal component
    baselines, interval-aware neighborhood assessment based on the local
    continuity meta-criterion (Lee and Verleysen, 2009,
    <doi:10.1016/j.neucom.2008.12.017>), plotting helpers, and reproducible
    analysis workflows are also included.
